  "id": "heart-rate-reactivity",
  "term": "heart rate reactivity",
  "definition": "Heart rate reactivity is the within-person change in heart rate that occurs while someone is doing a task, such as cognitive testing. In this context, it is used as an indicator of how strongly a person physiologically responds or engages during tasks of different difficulty.",
